w", "work_id": 95613, "role": "producer", "role_id": 1089, "is_primary": true}, {"id": 1978895, "title": "The Unfinished Dance", "work_id": 95612, "role": "producer", "role_id": 1089, "is_primary": true}, {"id": 1978848, "title": "Nancy goes to Rio", "work_id": 95566, "role": "producer", "role_id": 1089, "is_primary": true}], "also_known_as": "", "date_of_birth": "1901-09-19", "date_of_death": "1991-09-13", "genders": [], "languages": [], "places_of_operation": [{"id": 25, "name": "Hungary", "slug": "hungary"}], "biography": "Joseph Herman Pasternak (born József Paszternák; September 19, 1901 – September 13, 1991) was a Hungarian-American film producer in Hollywood. Pasternak spent the Hollywood \"Golden Age\" of musicals at Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer, producing many successful musicals with female singing stars like Deanna Durbin, Kathryn Grayson and Jane Powell, as well as swimmer/bathing beauty Esther Williams' films. He produced Judy Garland's final MGM film, Summer Stock, which was released in 1950, and some of Gene Kelly’s early breakthrough roles. Pasternak worked in the film industry for 45 years, from the later silent era until shortly past the end of the classical Hollywood cinema in the early 1960s.", "biography_author": "Wikidata", "date_of_biography": "2023-08-01T15:33:46.562152+10:00", "external_links": [{"id": 2397, "uri": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joe_Pasternak"}], "uuid": "c4e9acb3-f8dc-4203-ab88-0b5a63a8a0c9", "source": {"name": "Vernon", "slug": "vernon"}, "source_identifier": "22743", "external_references": [{"id": 10266, "source": {"name": "Wikidata", "slug": "wikidata"}, "source_identifier": "Q1691552"}, {"id": 10267, "source": {"name": "VIAF", "slug": "viaf"}, "source_identifier": "100242410"}, {"id": 10268, "source": {"name": "LOC Auth", "slug": "loc-auth"}, "source_identifier": "n85376897"}, {"id": 10269, "source": {"name": "WorldCat", "slug": "worldcat"}, "source_identifier": "lccn-n85376897"}], "date_modified": "2023-08-15T11:24:33.974676+10